    "text": "To find the length of the paint trail left by the tennis ball, we need to determine the length of the curve traced by the point \\((x(t), y(t))\\) as \\(t\\) varies from 0 to 4. The parametric equations for the position of the ball are given by:\n\\[ x(t) = 3t^2 - 9t - 5 \\]\n\\[ y(t) = t^2 - 3t + 2 \\]\nWe need to find the arc length of the curve described by these parametric equations over the interval \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\). The formula for the arc length \\(L\\) of a parametric curve \\((x(t), y(t))\\) from \\(t = a\\) to \\(t = b\\) is:\n\\[ L = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{dx}{dt} \\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac{dy}{dt} \\right)^2} \\, dt \\]\n\nFirst, we compute the derivatives \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\) and \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(3t^2 - 9t - 5) = 6t - 9 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(t^2 - 3t + 2) = 2t - 3 \\]\n\nNext, we substitute these derivatives into the arc length formula:\n\\[ L = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{(6t - 9)^2 + (2t - 3)^2} \\, dt \\]\n\nWe simplify the expression under the square root:\n\\[ (6t - 9)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81 \\]\n\\[ (2t - 3)^2 = 4t^2 - 12t + 9 \\]\n\\[ (6t - 9)^2 + (2t - 3)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81 + 4t^2 - 12t + 9 = 40t^2 - 120t + 90 \\]\n\\[ \\sqrt{40t^2 - 120t + 90} = \\sqrt{10(4t^2 - 12t + 9)} = \\sqrt{10(2t - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{10} |2t - 3| \\]\n\nSince \\(2t - 3\\) is negative for \\(0 \\le t < \\frac{3}{2}\\) and positive for \\(\\frac{3}{2} < t \\le 4\\), we can write:\n\\[ \\sqrt{10} |2t - 3| = \\sqrt{10} (3 - 2t) \\text{ for } 0 \\le t \\le \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\\[ \\sqrt{10} |2t - 3| = \\sqrt{10} (2t - 3) \\text{ for } \\frac{3}{2} < t \\le 4 \\]\n\nThus, the arc length integral splits into two parts:\n\\[ L = \\int_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\sqrt{10} (3 - 2t) \\, dt + \\int_{\\frac{3}{2}}^4 \\sqrt{10} (2t - 3) \\, dt \\]\n\nWe evaluate each integral separately:\n\\[ \\int_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\sqrt{10} (3 - 2t) \\, dt = \\sqrt{10} \\int_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} (3 - 2t) \\, dt = \\sqrt{10} \\left[ 3t - t^2 